<title>UK: UK's Hogg announces aid to beef farmers.</title>
<headline>UK's Hogg announces aid to beef farmers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK farm minister Douglas Hogg on Wednesday announced new measures to support UK beef farmers who have been hit by the crisis over mad cow disease.</p>
<p>Using EU money secured in October, he would be providing aid of 30 stg per suckler cow as a top up to the suckler cow premium, he told the National Farmers Union annual general meeting.</p>
<p>From the same source, 2.5 million sterling would be allotted for promotional activities. &quot;This, I think, will be widely welcomed across the industry,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Domestic confidence in British beef was already much restored, he said. &quot;Household consumption, especially of prime cuts, is now close to pre-crisis levels.&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Prices in the livestock markets have recovered to 1.03 stg per kilo or &quot;about 15 per cent down on this time last year,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
